      "{\"explanation\":\"The colorbar shows a reverse grayscale: the top end is nearly white and the bottom end is nearly black. In Matplotlib, the grayscale colormap that maps high values to dark and low values to light is 'gray'. Reversing it to match white at the top and black at the bottom gives 'Greys_r'.\"}\n",
      "Q: You are a helpful assistant that can analyze images. Assume this is a figure made with matplotlib in Python. Examples of matplotlib colormaps are \"rainbow\" or \"Reds\". What is the colormap that was used in this figure? Please format the output as a json as {\"colormap\":\"\"} to store the matplotlib colormap used in the figure.\n",
