      "{\"explanation\":\"The main plotting area is approximately 4 units wide for every 3 units tall (width and height look proportional to 4/3 \u2248 1.33). This matches a common 4:3 figure aspect ratio.\"}\n",
      "Q: You are a helpful assistant that can analyze images.  What is the aspect ratio of this figure? Please format the output as a json as {\"aspect ratio\":\"\"} to store the aspect ratio of the plot.\n",
      "   ground truth: 1.06771\n",
      "   LMM answer:   aspect ratio: 4:3\n",
      "                 explanation: The main plotting area is approximately 4 units wide for every 3 units tall (width and height look proportional to 4/3 \u2248 1.33). This matches a common 4:3 figure aspect ratio.\n",
      "   [rebuilt from \"raw answer\" -- stored Response held only an unparsed str]\n",
      "----------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
      "\n",
      "Raw Answer:\n",
      "{\"titles\":[\"\"]} \n",
      "\n",
      "{\"explanation\":\"I inspected the figure for a conventional plot title at the top or any prominent title text. The image shows axis labels (e.g., \u201cDec\u201d, \u201cRa\u201d) and a rotated colorbar label (\u201clog V [1/FREQ]\u201d) but no clear title text for the plot itself. Therefore, the title is denoted as an empty string.\"}\n",
      "Q: You are a helpful assistant that can analyze images.  What is the title of the plot in this figure? Please format the output as a json as {\"titles\":[]}, where the list holds the title of the plot as its only element.  If the plot does not have a title, then denote this by an empty string in the list.  Please format any formulas in the title in a Python LaTeX string (for example 'Light $\\\\alpha$'). \n",
      "   ground truth: [(empty)]\n",
