      "   [rebuilt from \"raw answer\" -- stored Response held only an unparsed str]\n",
      "----------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
      "\n",
      "Raw Answer:\n",
      "{\"xlabels\":[\"Ra\"]}\n",
      "\n",
      "{\"explanation\":\"The x-axis title appears centered below the main plot and reads \\\"Ra\\\".\"}\n",
      "Q: You are a helpful assistant that can analyze images.  What is the x-axis title of the plot in this figure? Please format the output as a json as {\"xlabels\":[]}, where the list holds the x-axis title of the plot as its only element. If the plot does not have an x-axis title, then denote this by an empty string in the list.  Please format any formulas in the title in a Python LaTeX string (for example 'Light $\\\\alpha$'). \n",
      "   ground truth: [Ra]\n",
      "   LMM answer:   xlabels: [Ra]\n",
      "                 explanation: The x-axis title appears centered below the main plot and reads \"Ra\".\n",
      "   [rebuilt from \"raw answer\" -- stored Response held only an unparsed str]\n",
      "----------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
      "\n",
