      "{\"ylabels\":[\"Dec\"]}\n",
      "\n",
      "{\"explanation\":\"The plot has a vertical axis on the left labeled \\\"Dec\\\" (declination). No other y-axis title is shown for the main heatmap.\"}\n",
      "Q: You are a helpful assistant that can analyze images.  What is the y-axis title of the plot in this figure? Please format the output as a json as {\"ylabels\":[]}, where the list holds the y-axis title of the plot as its only element. If the plot does not have an y-axis title, then denote this by an empty string in the list.  Please format any formulas in the title in a Python LaTeX string (for example 'Light $\\\\alpha$'). \n",
      "   ground truth: [Dec]\n",
      "   LMM answer:   ylabels: [Dec]\n",
      "                 explanation: The plot has a vertical axis on the left labeled \"Dec\" (declination). No other y-axis title is shown for the main heatmap.\n",
      "   [rebuilt from \"raw answer\" -- stored Response held only an unparsed str]\n",
      "----------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
      "\n",
